  <p class="cu-statement">Present landforms record the processes that produced them, so a landscape can be read as evidence of its own history.</p>
  <p class="gq-label">Questions that get you there</p>
  <ul class="guiding-questions">
    <li><span class="gq-type">Factual</span> Which processes shape a coast, a river channel, and a floodplain, and over what timescales?</li>
    <li><span class="gq-type">Conceptual</span> How can a landform that took ten thousand years to make constrain a decision made this year?</li>
    <li><span class="gq-type">Debatable</span> Should an urban river be channelized for flood control, or restored for the buffer it used to provide?</li>
  </ul>
</div>

